x86_64-linux  The C1 forms, and nothing else: every other name, the copy assignments included, agrees with clang. clang emits only the base-object C2 form of a constructor defined inside its class, and of an implicit one, on this target, where cxx1 emits the complete-object C1 beside it - the fact implicit-move.nonames and move-constructor.nonames already record. W's constructor is implicit, so moving the written ones out of line would not answer it. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree name for name.
